		"notes": {
			"techniques": "The dimple keeps the patty from doming as the edges contract. Salting only just before cooking keeps the texture loose.",
			"chemistry": "Salt mixed into ground meat dissolves myosin and makes it sausage-like and springy, which is why it goes on the surface at the last minute. Ground beef should reach 71 °C because surface bacteria get mixed throughout.",
			"variations": "A thick, juicy grilled patty. The smash burger has thin, crusty patties, and the Juicy Lucy hides the cheese inside."
